One fine summer afternoon a few weeks after this picture was taken at the Art Museum I made our own little museum on a side street. I don’t remember how much we paid for these, but I do recall a feeling of accomplishment looking back through all the doors. Not many people were taking about 30 seconds to look in the windows before hurrying on their way. We went outside and watched the passers-by as the streets filled for evening.
